---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Driver usage"
   summary="The driver gives you direct control over VoiceOver, NVDA, or the virtual screen reader. Start a session, navigate elements, send keystrokes, and read spoken output."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>When to use the driver</h2>
      <p>
         Use <code>drive</code> when you need low-level control: navigating items, sending keyboard
         chords, entering interaction mode, reading spoken output, and capturing logs. For repeatable
         checks, consider using a <a href="/pattern-execution">named pattern</a> instead.
      </p>
      <p>
         See the <a href="/workflows#drive-a-session">driver workflow</a> for a guided walkthrough.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Basic session</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 drive start --target virtual --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/landmarks.html --json
a1 drive next --session drv_example --json
a1 drive read --session drv_example --json
a1 drive stop --session drv_example --json</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Available actions</h2>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>start</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>stop</code><span>Create, inspect, and tear down a session.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>next</code>, <code>previous</code>, <code>interact</code>, <code>stop-interacting</code><span>Navigate through elements and switch interaction modes.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>key</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>click-current-item</code><span>Send keystrokes, type text, and click elements.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>read</code>, <code>logs</code>, <code>clear-logs</code>, <code>checkpoint</code><span>Read spoken output, view session logs, and create checkpoints.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Persistent vs. ephemeral sessions</h2>
      <p>
         Persistent sessions keep the full transcript, checkpoints, and state together across multiple
         commands. Use the <code>--ephemeral</code> flag for quick one-off actions.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Transcripts and verdicts</h2>
      <p>
         A driver transcript records what the screen reader said during a session. To produce a
         conformance verdict from that evidence, use the <a href="/verification-semantics">verification</a> layer.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
